WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.600
OpenAI is testing private safety processing that keeps frontier model interactions off limits

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:09.800
to staff while still catching risks across long agent sessions.

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:13.820
This is Models &amp; Agents, episode 147.

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:18.560
OpenAI previewed private safety processing for frontier models.

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:24.100
The system flags risks across related interactions in longer autonomous workflows.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:29.240
It does so without giving OpenAI staff access to the underlying content.

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:34.400
The previews sits alongside the company's continued zero data retention offering.

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:40.700
Builders working with extended agent sessions now have an explicit path to stronger safety controls

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:43.360
that do not require sharing raw data.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:50.860
The approach directly addresses the scaling challenge of monitoring multi-turn tool use and memory heavy conversations.

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:55.280
Watch for how the feature integrates with existing API workflows.

00:00:55.680 --> 00:01:02.300
On the safety track we covered yesterday, this moves the open question of evaluation standardization forward

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:05.320
by testing private review at frontier scale.

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:13.200
Kneebert is a domain specific encoder trained on 8.3 million sentences across nine northeast Indian languages,

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:15.060
plus Hindi and English.

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:19.940
It uses weighted sampling and a custom sentence piece unigram tokenizer.

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:26.320
The model delivers 15.97 times lower average perplexity than IndicBert V2.

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:31.100
It also shows 7.64 times lower perplexity than Muriel.

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:35.940
Tokenization fertility improves 1.5 times over Embert.

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:40.520
Downstream gains appear on part of speech tagging for three of the languages.

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:46.360
Researchers release the model, test sets, and corpus under CC by 4.0.

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:54.260
Sutra is a morphology aware tokenizer that preserves Akshara Indivisibility for Hindi, Marathi, and Gujarati.

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:57.760
It penalizes merges across morphological boundaries.

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:08.060
The tokenizer records peak gains of 14.7% in boundary F1 and 34% semantic recoverability on Hindi over standard BPE.

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:13.720
It delivers an average 8.08 char F2 improvement in machine translation.

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:19.140
The team also released a new morphological segmentation data set for the three languages.

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:25.620
Long novel provides a bilingual Chinese and English benchmark built from 29 Chinese novels,

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:31.560
ranging from 16,000 to 100,000 tokens, plus book some chapter data.

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:40.600
It defines 8 hallucination types and uses multi-model arbitration, plus entity reference generation, to create balanced test cases.

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:44.180
Researchers release the data set and evaluation code.

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:52.860
Nine emotion centroid extracts a single valence direction from nine emotion category names, plus 50 short paragraphs per emotion.

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:58.820
The resulting axis captures 93% of supervised performance on SST2.

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:04.160
It transfers to vision, audio, and brain recordings without target modality labels.

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:14.140
A two parameter classifier trained only on text reaches AUC 0.961 on images and 0.828 on brain data.

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:19.420
The persona guided framework runs two LLMs in a training free loop.

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:29.180
A user agent expresses a target big five personality, while a system agent adapts to complete hotel or restaurant tasks from the SGD data set.

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:36.220
Oracle personality knowledge improves constraint satisfaction and user satisfaction, but reduces truthfulness.

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:40.980
Q-based inference offers the best reliability performance trade-off.

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:49.580
The study evaluates GPT 40, Quinn 3 next ADB, and Gemini 2.0 flash across all trade pulls.

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:54.980
Stocks talk converts spoken financial screening requests into validated SQL.

00:03:54.980 --> 00:04:05.120
It uses streaming ASR, retrieval augmented constraint extraction, schema grounded generation, and rule based validation inside an interactive dashboard.

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:18.540
A 150 prompt benchmark shows retrieval grounding and human in the loop verification, raise constraint accuracy, SQL executability, and multi-turn stability over plain LLM baselines.

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:25.820
Simon Willison released notes and a GitHub research repo on running untrusted code in a small VMM sandbox.

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:30.540
The setup tested cloud code in a restricted environment that lacks dev KVM.

00:04:31.720 --> 00:04:37.800
The work provides concrete configuration details for builders who need isolated execution for agent tool calls.

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:56.100
A 3-day benchmark on a 4090 laptop plus 7900 XTX EGPU over Thunderbolt 4 reached 27 tokens per second generation and full 262K context on Quinn 3.827 BQ6K XL.

00:04:56.820 --> 00:05:05.280
The author filed an upstream issue on multi-GPU MTP pre-fill penalties and published the LLM tuner repo used for the experiments.

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:11.300
Google is offering eligible students a full year of Gemini AI access at no cost.

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:18.060
The program targets higher education users and provides the same model capabilities available to paid subscribers.

00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:27.820
FD-KVC maintains dual scoring channels per KV pair using cumulative attention and recency weighted relevance with temporal decay.

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:31.900
It uses an ownership loss to drive adaptive learning rates.

00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:44.620
Across 600 dialogue test sets, it outperforms H2O by 6.7% on late-turn alignment and adapts to topic shifts 3.6 times faster while running entirely on CPU.

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:49.260
Okay, let's pop the hood on KV cache eviction under topic drift.

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:54.440
Everyone treats KV cache eviction as a simple keep the most attended tokens rule.

00:05:54.440 --> 00:06:03.820
In practice, the decision surface changes as soon as the conversation topic shifts because attention mass from earlier turns stops predicting future utility.

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:07.420
The core insight is that importance is not stationary.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:14.220
A token that was heavily attended during the first topic can become irrelevant noise once the user changes subject.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:22.940
Dual channel scoring separates aggregate attention from a recency weighted relevance signal that decays unless reinforced by new matches.

00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:30.520
Adding an ownership loss term prevents the eviction policy from oscillating when the same entities reappear later in the dialogue.

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:41.080
The practical tradeoff is modest CPU overhead for the extra scoring pass versus measurable gains in late-turn alignment and faster recovery after topic changes.

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:50.100
Teams running long multi-turn agents should prefer dual channel or ownership aware eviction once context exceeds roughly 50K tokens.

00:06:50.100 --> 00:06:56.000
Single signal LRU or H2O remains adequate for shorter single topic sessions.

00:06:56.580 --> 00:07:01.180
Test NE BERT on any Northeast Indian language tagging or retrieval task.

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:05.540
The released weights and corpus make it a drop-in low resource baseline.

00:07:06.220 --> 00:07:14.740
Run the Sutra tokenizer against your current BPE pipeline on Hindi or Gujarati MT data to measure the reported Char F2 lift.

00:07:14.740 --> 00:07:23.380
Add long novel to your long context summarization eval, harness to surface hallucination patterns that news or paper benchmarks miss.

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:32.740
Try the final llama.cpp flag set from the 40GB mixed GPU benchmark on your own Quen 3.827b workload.

00:07:33.420 --> 00:07:40.560
Prototype a dual channel KV eviction policy in your dialogue agent using the FDKBC description as a starting point.

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:47.140
Further details are expected on open AI's private safety processing rollout and integration surface.

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:53.360
Additional low resource Indic model releases are already signaled in the NE BERT and Sutra papers.

00:07:54.200 --> 00:08:00.960
More llama.cpp multi-GPU and MTP fixes are likely after the file issue receives community attention.

